  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Remove ends from lemons and discard. Remove lemon peel with a knife and set aside.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Quarter lemons and squeeze juice and pulp into a bowl. Remove and discard white membrane and seeds.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Break the peel into half inch chunks and place the peel, juice and pulp in a blender or food processor. Cover and process until coarsely chopped.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add sugar to the lemon mixture. Mix well and let stand for 30 minutes.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in milk and then strain lemon mixture.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add club soda and food coloring if desired. Serve immediately in sugar-rimmed glasses if desired.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "Plan ahead on how you will strain the lemon mixture with the rind in it. I ended up using a colander because the mixture was too thick for a strainer. I tripled this recipe for the home group so it took about an hour to prepare. Adele"
